// Title: Potential DLL Sideloading Of DbgModel.DLL
// Sigma ID: fef394cd-f44d-4040-9b18-95d92fe278c0
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Gary Lobermier
// Date: 2024-07-11 | Modified: 2024-07-22
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, execution, stealth, T1574.001
// Description: Detects potential DLL sideloading of "DbgModel.dll"
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate applications loading their own versions of the DLL mentioned in this rule
// References:
//   - https://hijacklibs.net/entries/microsoft/built-in/dbgmodel.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/image_load/image_load_side_load_dbgmodel.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceImageLoadEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\dbgmodel.dll" and (not((FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\System32\\" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\WinSxS\\"))) and (not((FolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files\\WindowsApps\\Microsoft.WinDbg_" or (FolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Windows Kits\\" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files\\Windows Kits\\"))))
